From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:33:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] node: pin self-hosted runtimes to the October security
 release

Select Node.js 24.22.1 for local execution, backend and dashboard images,
and the development container. Both image recipes already derive their
exact NodeSource package from .nvmrc, so pinned resident executors inherit
the same patched binary without another runtime version selector.

Regenerate only Node's mise lock entries, including available checksums
for all seven platforms. Align SDK CI and update the runtime adoption
notes while preserving the executor's existing Node 24 compatibility rule.

Validated official download metadata and checksums, image and NodeSource
package availability, configuration syntax and local binary startup.
Image builds and replacement of running services remain separate.

[skip ci]
